<title>USA: Eli Lilly unit to invest $40 mln in center.</title>
<headline>Eli Lilly unit to invest $40 mln in center.</headline>
<dateline>DURHAM, N.C. 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eli Lilly and Co unit Sphinx Pharmaceuticals said Tuesday it will invest about $40 million to build a new research center in Durham County, N.C.</p>
<p>Sphinx said it currently employs 90 people and expects that number to grow to 150 as the new center is completed and eventually to grow to 200.  </p>
<p>Work on the new center is expected to begin in July and to be completed in the second half of 1998.</p>
<p>Eli Lilly is a global research-based pharmaceutical company.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
